Timberland's Timberloop program enables customers to return worn products for 10% off future purchases. In partnership with ReCircled, items in good condition are refurbished and resold on Timberland's secondhand site; beyond-repair products are disassembled for component recycling. Timberland designed the Timberloop Trekker specifically for circularity, featuring outsoles removable without damaging uppers, enabling each component to enter appropriate recycling streams. The program exemplifies thoughtful product design for end-of-life management: modular construction, transparent material streams, and accessible reverse logistics enable scalable take-back. By closing loops at product design stage and partnering with specialized recyclers, Timberloop demonstrates how major brands can operationalize circular principles.